
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>CSS Filters and Shadows</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial;margin:0;padding:20px;background:#f1f5f9;color:#1e293b}
section{max-width:900px;margin:20px auto;padding:20px;background:white;border-radius:8px}
.demo{display:inline-block;background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:18px;margin:12px;border-radius:6px}
.gray{filter:grayscale(100%)}
.blur{filter:blur(2px)}
.bright{filter:brightness(1.4)}
.dark{filter:brightness(.65)}
.contrast{filter:contrast(180%)}
.sepia{filter:sepia(100%)}
.invert{filter:invert(100%)}
.saturate{filter:saturate(250%)}
.shadow{box-shadow:6px 6px 12px #94a3b8}
.inner{box-shadow:inset 0 0 10px #0f172a}
.text-shadow{text-shadow:3px 3px 4px #94a3b8}
.multiple{box-shadow:0 4px 8px #94a3b8,0 10px 20px #cbd5e1}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}
td,th{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:9px;text-align:left}
th{background:#dbeafe}
code{color:#9a3412}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<section>
<h1>CSS Filters & Shadows</h1>
<p><b>Filter:</b> Changes the visual appearance of an element.</p>
<p><b>Shadow:</b> Adds a shadow behind a box or text.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Part 1: CSS Filter Examples</h2>
<div class="demo">Original</div>
<div class="demo gray">Grayscale</div>
<div class="demo blur">Blur</div>
<div class="demo bright">Brightness</div>
<div class="demo dark">Dark</div>
<div class="demo contrast">Contrast</div>
<div class="demo sepia">Sepia</div>
<div class="demo invert">Invert</div>
<div class="demo saturate">Saturate</div>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Part 2: CSS Box Shadows</h2>
<div class="demo shadow">Box Shadow</div>
<div class="demo inner">Inset Shadow</div>
<div class="demo multiple">Multiple Shadows</div>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Part 3: CSS Text Shadow</h2>
<h1 class="text-shadow">Beautiful Text</h1>
<p class="text-shadow">This paragraph has a text shadow.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Quick Reference Table</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Property / Value</th><th>Simple explanation</th></tr>
<tr><td>filter: grayscale(100%)</td><td>Removes color.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: blur(2px)</td><td>Makes content blurry.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: brightness(1.4)</td><td>Makes content brighter.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: contrast(180%)</td><td>Increases contrast.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: sepia(100%)</td><td>Gives a brown, old-photo effect.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: invert(100%)</td><td>Inverts colors.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: saturate(250%)</td><td>Increases color intensity.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: opacity(50%)</td><td>Makes content partly transparent.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: hue-rotate(90deg)</td><td>Changes the colors' hue.</td></tr>
<tr><td>filter: drop-shadow()</td><td>Adds a shadow following an image's shape.</td></tr>
<tr><td>box-shadow</td><td>Adds a shadow around a box.</td></tr>
<tr><td>text-shadow</td><td>Adds a shadow to text.</td></tr>
<tr><td>inset</td><td>Makes a box shadow appear inside the box.</td></tr>
</table>
<p><b>Example:</b> <code>box-shadow: 4px 4px 10px #999;</code></p>
<p><b>Order:</b> box-shadow values are horizontal offset, vertical offset, blur radius, and color.</p>
</section>
</body>
</html>
